# R6a-EX1 evidence (orchestrator, 2026-10-06): r1_04_alloc_core_drop_stack_pressure under --cfg numa_shim_mock
# cause: the inline numa-shim mock call log (CALLS_CAP=4096 x ~32 B ~ 128 KiB) sits in every thread's static TLS; glibc carves static TLS out of the thread stack,
# so the 64 KiB-stack threads of this test had no usable stack. Fix: commit 784bdfdf (CALLS_CAP 4096 -> 256). CI run 37399933378 (job "test (gated bodies + all-features)") was red before the fix and green after.

## WSL (Ubuntu), CALLS_CAP=4096 (before the fix): RUSTFLAGS="--cfg numa_shim_mock" cargo test --all-features --test r1_04_alloc_core_drop_stack_pressure
